WEBVTT

00:00:59.287 --> 00:01:02.579
But after the United States has
abolished this system in 1971,

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:06.663
the dollar has become
what is called a fiduciary currency,

00:01:06.663 --> 00:01:09.454
that is to say linked to
no external resources

00:01:09.454 --> 00:01:12.413
but rather relying entirely on the
government policy

00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:14.746
to decide the quantity
of change to print.

00:01:14.746 --> 00:01:18.038
So what is the power of our
government that sets this policy?

00:01:18.038 --> 00:01:20.788
The executive, the legislature,
or the judiciary?

00:01:20.788 --> 00:01:23.038
The answer is surprising:
none of them.

00:01:23.038 --> 00:01:25.288
In fact, monetary policy
is established

00:01:25.288 --> 00:01:27.621
by a System of
Independent Federal Reserve,

00:01:27.621 --> 00:01:29.121
otherwise called the FED,

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.496
made up of 12 regional banks